{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["R33", "U7"],
      "pins": ["U7.27", "R33.1", "R33.2"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The current-sense resistor R33 (110 mΩ) is wired with BOTH terminals on the GND net, and U7's B-bridge current-sense pin BRB (pin 27) is tied directly to GND. There is no /BRB_NB-type net as there is for the other two drivers.",
      "expected": "R33 should sit between U7.BRB (pin 27) and GND, exactly as R31 does for U6 (net /BRB_NA = R31.1 ↔ U6.27) and R35 does for U5 (net /BRB_pH = R35.1 ↔ U5.27). The spec lists 'its own current-sense resistor pair (R30–R35, 110 mΩ)' for each TMC2209.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"75\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"R33\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"R33\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"BRB\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"21\") (name \"/BRB_{NA}\") (node (ref \"R31\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"BRB\") (pintype \"input\")))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R33 0 0 110m"}
      ],
      "impact": "The Nutrient-B (U7) B-phase bridge has no usable current-sense resistor: BRB is hard-wired to GND, so the TMC2209 senses ~0 V and cannot regulate the B-coil current, defeating current limiting and stallGuard sensing for that motor and risking overcurrent / erratic dosing-pump operation. It also makes the design asymmetric with the other two drivers.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain one clear anomaly: current-sense resistor R33 has both terminals on GND and U7's BRB pin is shorted straight to ground, removing the B-phase current-sense path for the Nutrient-B TMC2209 while U5/U6 have proper sense resistors (R35/R31)."
}

